{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>Cherubim.</b> They have the form of a child's face." "<b>Of beaten work shall you make them.</b> That you shall not make them on their own and join them to the top of the cover after their making, like the work of goldsmiths, which is called שולד״יר בְּלַעַז — but rather: cast much gold at the start of making the cover, and beat with hammer and mallet in the middle, so that heads protrude upward, and shape the cherubim in the protrusion of its edges." "<b>Beaten.</b> בטד״ץ בְּלַעַז — as in ״דָּא לְדָא נָקְשָׁן״ (Daniel 5)." "<b>The ends of the cover.</b> The top of the cover."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {1 "the la'az שולד״יר is Old French souldier, 'to solder/fashion by joining'", 2 "the la'az בטד״ץ is Old French betacier, 'attached/joined'"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:54:29.261787192Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}